    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0184" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/1804½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">8 July, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: My clear judgment about
                        this<anchor n="1" xml:id="d97-f1"/> is, that it is not wise to take such
                    action piecemeal about the items of a final settlement. Our attitude is clearly
                    spoken by our actions. The world has no doubt where we stand, and we have
                    already recognized the representatives of a Polish State. If we are to be
                    definite in the case of this particular national aspiration, why not in the case
                    of others, and where shall we stop, definition being at each step increasingly
                    difficult.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
